<body>
    <h1>Text Recognition</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"TextRecognition-Introduction">Introduction</h2>
<p>Have you ever needed to scan a document or turn an image with text into =
something you could edit on your computer? Maybe you=E2=80=99ve taken a pho=
to of a piece of paper or used a printer with a scanner, but how does print=
ed or handwritten text turn into an editable file? That=E2=80=99s where <st=
rong>OCR</strong> and <strong>ICR</strong> technologies come in.</p>
<p>These technologies help turn images with text, whether from printed docu=
ments or even handwritten notes, into digital files that can be easily mani=
pulated on a computer.</p>
<p>For example, OCR can read and convert printed text, while ICR goes even =
further by recognizing handwritten letters. This really helps in lots of ar=
eas like accounting, document organization, reading forms filled out by han=
d, and using that data in our apps.</p>
<p>So let=E2=80=99s go into a more direct explanation of OCR:</p>
<h3 id=3D"TextRecognition-1.What=E2=80=99sOCR?">1. What=E2=80=99s <strong>O=
CR?</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>OCR</strong> stands for <em>Optical Character Recognition</em>.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>It=E2=80=99s a technology that converts <strong>text images</strong> (li=
ke photos of documents or scans) into <strong>editable text</strong> on a c=
omputer.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If you take a picture of a page from a book, O=
CR can identify the words in the image and turn them into text you can copy=
, paste, and edit on your computer.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"TextRecognition-2.HowdoesOCRwork?">2. How does <strong>OCR work?<=
/strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>OCR analyzes an image and <strong>recognizes the characters</strong> in =
it by comparing the shapes of letters to a database of known fonts.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Then, it turns the recognized shapes into digital characters that you ca=
n manipulate like any regular text.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"TextRecognition-3.What=E2=80=99sOCRusedfor?">3. What=E2=80=99s <s=
trong>OCR used for?</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Document scanning:</strong> Converting physical paper into digit=
al files.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>License plate reading:</strong> Recognizing numbers on car plate=
s.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Form and invoice processing:</strong> Makes accounting and data =
autofill easier.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"TextRecognition-4.AppleandOCR">4. Apple and OCR</h3>
<p><strong>Text Recognition</strong> has been part of several technologies =
developed by <strong>Apple</strong>, especially in products like the <stron=
g>iPhone</strong>, <strong>iPad</strong>, and <strong>macOS</strong>. Here =
are some examples of how Apple has built text recognition into their ecosys=
tem:</p>
<p><strong>Live Text</strong> Live Text was introduced in <strong>iOS 15</s=
trong> and <strong>macOS Monterey</strong>. It lets users interact with tex=
t inside images. Using OCR technology, <strong>Live Text</strong> recognize=
s text in images and turns it into editable content.</p>
<p>Users can, for example:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em>Copy:</em> Copy the text to paste into another app like Notes or Mes=
sages.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Select All:</em> Select all the text in the frame.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Look Up:</em> See personalized web suggestions.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Translate:</em> Translate text.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Search the Web:</em> Search the selected text online.</p></li>
<li>
<p><em>Share:</em> Share the text using AirDrop, Messages, Mail, or other o=
ptions.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Apple Notes and Photos</strong> In the <strong>Notes</strong> an=
d <strong>Photos</strong> apps, Apple also uses OCR to detect text within i=
mages. In the Photos app, if you take a picture of a handwritten list or a =
poster, the text is recognized and becomes searchable.</p>
<p><strong>Vision</strong> The <strong>Apple Vision Framework</strong>, int=
roduced in <strong>iOS 11</strong>, offers developers a set of tools to bui=
ld apps that involve image processing and text recognition. The framework i=
ncludes <strong>OCR</strong>, making it easy for developers to integrate te=
xt recognition features into their apps. This can be used to scan documents=
, read text from signs, books, etc.</p>
<h3 id=3D"TextRecognition-5.ImplementingLiveText">5. Implementing Live Text=
</h3>
<p>A quick example of how to use Live Text in our apps is by using VisionKi=
t. With a few steps, we can capture text from images or recognize it throug=
h the camera.</p>
<p>To allow the app to use the camera, you=E2=80=99ll need to add a privacy=
 setting in the app=E2=80=99s target by following these steps:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>In Xcode, click on the application.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Next, click on the target and then go to Info.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Then, in the last option, add the field "Privacy - Camera Usage Descript=
ion=E2=80=9D and next to it, write the message that=E2=80=99ll be shown whe=
n asking for permission.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>To <strong>interact with text from an image</strong>, we need to impleme=
nt an image analyzer that, through VisionKit, will extract the information =
we need by recognizing the text from the image.</p>
<p>In this example, we=E2=80=99re using a <code>UIViewRepresentable</code> =
to display image on the main screen and let us select text using the analyz=
er.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">struct L=
iveTextUIImageView: UIViewRepresentable {
    var image: UIImage
    let analyzer =3D ImageAnalyzer()
    let interaction =3D ImageAnalysisInteraction()
    let imageView =3D ResizableImageView()
    func makeUIView(context: Context) -&gt; UIImageView {
        imageView.image =3D image
        imageView.addInteraction(interaction)
        imageView.contentMode =3D .scaleAspectFit
        return imageView
    }
   =20
    func updateUIView(_ uiView: UIImageView, context: Context) {
        Task {
            do {
                let configuration =3D ImageAnalyzer.Configuration([.text])
                if let image =3D imageView.image {
                    let analysis =3D try await analyzer.analyze(image, conf=
iguration: configuration)
                    interaction.analysis =3D analysis
                    interaction.preferredInteractionTypes =3D .textSelectio=
n
                }
            } catch {
                print(error.localizedDescription)
            }
        }
    }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Once the analyzer lets us select the text, we can send that text to the =
pasteboard or use it for whatever purposes needed in our application.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">var body=
: some View {
      NavigationStack {
          VStack {
              LiveTextUIImageView(image: imageToScan)
              Text("Select text and copy it")
              Button("Dismiss") {
                  if let string =3D pastboard.string {
                      if !string.isEmpty {
                          scannedText =3D string
                      }
                  }
                  dismiss()
              }
              .buttonStyle(.borderedProminent)
          }
          .navigationTitle("Copy Text")
          .navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)
          .onAppear {
              pastboard.string =3D ""
          }
      }
  }</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>To <strong>interact with text from the camera</strong>, it=E2=80=99s nec=
essary to implement a scanner that, through VisionKit, will extract the inf=
ormation we need by recognizing the text that=E2=80=99s being shown live th=
rough the camera.</p>
<p>In this example, we=E2=80=99re using a <code>UIViewControllerRepresentab=
le</code> to help manage the process of retrieving the information. It incl=
udes a <code>Coordinator</code> to capture the information we want from the=
 camera.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">struct D=
ataScanner: UIViewControllerRepresentable {
    @Binding var scannedText: String
    @Binding var liveScan: Bool
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">class Co=
ordinator: NSObject, DataScannerViewControllerDelegate {
    var parent: DataScanner
    init(parent: DataScanner) {
        self.parent =3D parent
    }
   =20
    func dataScanner(_ dataScanner: DataScannerViewController, didTapOn ite=
m: RecognizedItem) {
        switch item {
        case .text(let text):
            parent.scannedText =3D text.transcript
            parent.liveScan =3D false
        default:
            break
        }
    }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>For both methods, all you need to do is return the extracted information=
 to the variables you want to use in your app and keep going.</p>
<h2 id=3D"TextRecognition-Conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p><strong>Text Recognition</strong> plays a big role in how we deal with s=
canned documents and images. By turning visual content into editable and se=
archable text, these technologies make it easier to organize, search, and w=
ork with information. And when paired with smart code, they can speed up al=
l kinds of data collection processes.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
